  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "The time taken by an object to slide down <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> rough inclined plane is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi></math> times as it takes to slide down a perfectly smooth <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> incline plane. The coefficient of kinetic friction between the object and the incline plane is:",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "iNTKM",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow></mfrac></msqrt></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "D5A7v",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></msqrt></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "FMeLz",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "2uI6M",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math>",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let angle of inclination is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>45</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>.</p><p>Then, acceleration along the incline in case of smooth incline will be,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>g</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>.</p><p>In case of rough incline, kinetic friction will act against the direction of motion. Normal force acting on the object will be&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi></math>. Therefore,&nbsp;acceleration along the incline in case of rough incline will be,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>sin</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>cos</mi><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>g</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></math>.</p><p>Now as per question,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math></p><p>and as the displacement covered is the same in both case,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mi>g</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mi>g</mi><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><msqrt><mn>2</mn></msqrt></mfrac></mrow></mfenced><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><msubsup><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msup><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mfrac></math></p>",
    "image": null
